<title>FRANCE: LVMH H1 net attrib pre-excep rises.</title>
<headline>LVMH H1 net attrib pre-excep rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   1,543  vs	   1,464</p>
<p>    Operating				    2,617  vs	   2,921</p>
<p>	- champagnes and wines		   167  vs	     145</p>
<p>	- cognac and spirits		     796  vs	     790</p>
<p>	- luggage and leather goods	  1,724  vs	   1,717</p>
<p>	- perfumes and beauty products	  70  vs	     380</p>
<p>	- other			     loss   140  vs	loss 111</p>
<p>    Turnover				    13,365  vs	  13,340</p>
<p>NOTE - LVMH gave its first-half results in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the drop in operating profit was due mainly to the performance of the perfumes and beauty products division which is battling counterfeit sales.</p>
<p>First-half net attributable profit excluding exceptionals rose 5.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
